A new metal–organic framework $\{[\mathrm{Zn}_{2}(\mathrm{bpta})(\mathrm{bpy-ee})(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O})_{2}]\cdot\mathrm{x}\ s\mathrm{olve}\}_{n}\left(\bf{1}\right)|\psi_{\mathrm{X}}\cdot\mathrm{x}\ s\mathrm{olve}\rangle_{\mathrm{}}$ $\mathrm{\partial\cdotH_{4}b p t a=}$ biphenyl- $^{2,2^{\prime},6,6^{\prime},}$ - tetracarboxylic acid and bpy- $\cdot\mathrm{ee}=1{,}2$ -bis(4-pyridyl)ethylene) has been obtained under hydrothermal condition, and structurally characterized by single-crystal X-ray diffraction. Complex 1 reveals a threedimensional (3D) ‘‘pillar-layered’’ framework with non-flexible linker, in which some different structure characters can be found compared to that of some related other ‘‘pillar-layered’’ MOFs based on flexible pillar linkers. It demonstrates the impact of the flexibility of pillar linker on the final structure in this system. In addition, the selective ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ adsorption performance of 1 was also investigated.
